D21's unreachable clamp and D36's never-filled cache.

The five that stayed open longest — D4, D8, D9, D10 and D11 — were parked not
because they were hard but because each altered something the user already saw,
so they needed a deliberate call rather than a drive-by fix. All five were then
decided together and fixed in one pass; see [§1.2](#12-the-five-parked-defects).

### 1.1 Fixed

**D118 — DEVDESK-201: Bubble Tea v2 features not adopted, what the migration found on the way, and what is still open. Decided for the first two lists, the rest to confirm.** **Plane:** DEVDESK-201,
42:**Render and View (Bubble Tea v2, DEVDESK-201).** A top-level view keeps
47:sets terminal state: `App.View()` wraps `App.Render()` and sets `AltScreen`
48:(`main.go` passes no `tea.WithAltScreen()`). The setup wizard is its own
49:program and sets `AltScreen` in its own `View()`. Components (datatable, forms,
```

**Render and View (Bubble Tea v2, DEVDESK-201).** A top-level view keeps
`Render() string` and wraps it: `View() tea.View { return tea.NewView(m.Render()) }`.
`app.Screen` is `tea.Model` plus `Render() string`; the router holds
`map[ViewType]Screen` and installs every view through the single `setView`,
which panics naming the view when a model has no `Render()`. Only the router
sets terminal state: `App.View()` wraps `App.Render()` and sets `AltScreen`
(`main.go` passes no `tea.WithAltScreen()`). The setup wizard is its own
